  "title": "Syllabus",
  "body": " Syllabus   Welcome to our course. In this Course we will introduce quadratic polynomials (Polynomials of degree 2). This course will quadratic expressions, equations and quadratic graphs.     Course Information  This is the syllabus for Introduction to polynomials: Quadratic equations and expressions for 2026. It is a foundational course on advanced polynomial functions.    Instructor  Mr. TONNY BLAIR tonnyblair858@gmail.com .    Course Description  course description from catalog    Prerequisite  Linear expressions and equations    Textbook and course materials     Mentor Core Mathematics Grade 10  James Stewart's Algebra and Trigonometry     Schaum's Outline College Algebra           Course Overview     Core Competency: Critical thinking and problem solving through mathematical modelling     Learning Outcomes: By the end of this module, the learners should be able to:   Identify and write quadratic expressions and equations.    Expand and factorize quadratic expressions using quadratic identities.    Form quadratic equations from real-life situations and solve quadratic equations using multiple methods.    Sketch and interpret quadratic graphs and apply quadratic concepts to real world scenarios.            Assessments and Evaluation     Formative Assessment    Daily Practice: Short problem sets covering each solving method    Peer Review: Students exchanging papers to verify step by step working.       Summative Assessment :   Practice Problems: Problem sets that blends real world applications of quadratic concepts    Olympiad Problems: Practice Olympiad problems that test mastery and application of concepts.         "
